# Cloudflare Workers custom response headers (Static Assets).
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# The Content-Security-Policy on every page already blocks all outbound
# connections, form submissions, and third-party scripts/styles/fonts via
# a <meta http-equiv> tag baked into the HTML — that travels with the file
# regardless of host and needs no change here.
#
# A <meta> CSP cannot express frame-ancestors (the HTML spec has browsers
# ignore that directive when set via <meta>), so nothing was stopping this
# site from being framed by another origin. This file adds that, plus a
# few baseline hardening headers GitHub Pages had no mechanism to set at
# all, and fixes a missing charset on non-HTML text files (this is what
# caused the mangled em dash in robots.txt).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

/*.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

/*.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8

/*.css
  Content-Type: text/css; charset=utf-8

/*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

/robots.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
